  faqs: [
    { question: "How does a Rohtak family actually kick this off?", answer: "By laying out the basics: programme or board, subject, level, exam session. That alone lets us build a shortlist, since Rohtak has no confirmed local IB or IGCSE school and being nearby was never going to be the deciding factor. A lesson slot gets fixed around your evening, the free trial runs first, and we adjust course if it doesn't land." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram cover both Cambridge and Edexcel IGCSE for Rohtak students?", answer: "It does, both online. Cambridge students get matched to their precise code and tier, say Mathematics 0580 Extended, and Edexcel students to their specification and Foundation or Higher tier, each taught using that specific board's past papers and mark schemes." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram do in-person home tuition in Rohtak, or is it online only?", answer: "Online only, and we'd rather be upfront than let anyone assume otherwise based on Rohtak sitting inside the wider NCR boundary. IB Gram's physical visits stop at Gurugram and select Delhi NCR pockets. What Rohtak gets is a live online lesson instead, video call and shared screen, delivered as genuine tuition rather than a stand-in for something unavailable." },
    { question: "What kind of fee should a Rohtak household plan for?", answer: "The programme, level, subject, session length and how current the tutor's experience is with that exact syllabus all factor in, and a number gets settled before your trial begins. HL Diploma subjects tend to run higher than MYP or IGCSE Core work. Online-only delivery removes any travel cost, and nothing is ever packaged as a term-long commitment." },
    { question: "That 'IB School' on Gohana Road, does it actually teach the IB?", answer: "It doesn't. The name is coincidental; the school runs a CBSE curriculum with no link to the International Baccalaureate. As far as we've confirmed, no school inside Rohtak teaches the real IB or Cambridge or Edexcel IGCSE, which is why families after an actual school tend to look toward Gurugram or Delhi." },
    { question: "Is there a hidden cost to the free trial lesson?", answer: "Not that we've built in anywhere. A live, online session on a real topic from the syllabus, free of charge, with zero obligation to book another. A short plan for month one follows, and the decision to continue, tweak something, or try someone new sits entirely with you." },
    { question: "Can a tutor be asked to draft any part of an Internal Assessment?", answer: "No, and that answer doesn't change regardless of how the ask is framed. What's on the table instead: sharpening a research question, walking through what an assessment criterion is genuinely looking for, reviewing how data was collected, marking a draft honestly. Actually producing the assessed text would violate IB integrity rules." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects get requested most often by Rohtak-linked households?", answer: "Both Maths tracks, Analysis and Approaches and Applications and Interpretation, at HL and SL, sit at the top, trailed by Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, with Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay support layered in wherever needed." },
    { question: "Does support extend below the Diploma years?", answer: "Across the entire continuum. MYP work tends to focus on criterion-based analysis in the sciences and Individuals and Societies, plus keeping a Personal Project journal on schedule. PYP work stays lighter: reading, writing, number sense and Exhibition research, delivered in sessions built for a shorter attention span." },
    { question: "Realistically, is a screen as good as a tutor physically present?", answer: "For Rohtak specifically, the comparison barely applies, since a local specialist in this exact syllabus isn't really an option to begin with, and physical visits aren't part of what's on offer here anyway. Online is the only format available, and a shared screen, live demonstrations and lessons you can replay still cover most of what in-person teaching provides, while opening the search to tutors from anywhere in India rather than just the local area." },
    { question: "What's the actual vetting bar before a tutor gets introduced?", answer: "Recent, hands-on teaching at that precise level, plus a demonstrated approach to IA supervision, matter more than any qualification listed on paper. Because Rohtak has no confirmed IB or IGCSE school to compare against, the search deliberately targets tutors who've taught this syllabus elsewhere in the country within the last year or two." },
    { question: "When's the smart time to bring a tutor on board?", answer: "As close to the start of the course as possible, Class 11 for the Diploma, Grade 9 for IGCSE, which buys time to fix gaps before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades all land together. Coming in later still helps, just with a plan tightened around the highest-value topics and past papers." },
    { question: "How rough is the switch from CBSE or the Haryana Board into IB or IGCSE?", answer: "It's one of the most frequent questions from families here, simply because no confirmed local school offers either curriculum to begin with. Content usually isn't the sticking point, the question style is: words like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' need to be taught directly, and getting a head start the summer before the switch makes a real difference to the first term." },
    { question: "Are weekend slots realistic, or is it weekday evenings by default?", answer: "Both are realistic. Weekday evenings work once the school day and any coaching classes are behind everyone, while weekend mornings suit households with more room to breathe. Scheduling factors in Rohtak's summer heat, the occasional foggy winter morning, and breaks like Diwali and Holi rather than treating them as surprises." },
    { question: "What if a tutor just isn't clicking with my child?", answer: "Say so, and a different tutor gets found. Check-ins every few weeks exist specifically to catch this before it drags on, and there's no contract forcing anyone to stick with a bad fit. Pausing entirely, or stopping altogether, remains an option at any point, no strings attached." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram hold any formal tie to a Rohtak school, or to the IB itself?", answer: "None whatsoever. Every school this page mentions, along with the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education and Pearson Edexcel, operates entirely independently of IB Gram. They're named purely to point toward where a genuine curriculum option exists, and tutoring follows that school's own calendar and the relevant board's published syllabus." },
  ],

